/* ============================================================
   ARCHIVUS — THE COUPS: the archive's own roll (v11).
   Hand-written. The systematic record — every coup attempt since
   1950 (Powell & Thyne) and every regime ended by force since 1789
   (V-Dem) — is the generated file src/data/coups-record.js; this
   file is the curated layer on top of it: the seizures worth
   knowing by name, from Athens to last year, each classed by
     kind  — how power was taken
     ideo  — the creed of those who took it (not of those they removed)
     goal  — what they said they were doing it for
     ok    — 1 took power and held it · 2 took it briefly or in part · 0 failed
   and each with a source (w = an English Wikipedia article title).
   list: [id, year, name, place, iso3 of the modern state, kind, ideo, goal, ok, text, w, disputed?]
   red/green cases: [id, route, conditions present, label?, outcome for the movement?] — the last two only where the
   roll entry is the coup made AGAINST the movement (an election won, then blocked).

   Classing is judgment. Most seizures mix motives; the class given
   is the plotters' own declared banner. Where calling an event a
   coup at all is disputed, the entry says so (last field = 1).
   ============================================================ */
