    never: "What never happened is as instructive. No communist party has taken power by force in an established democracy with a functioning army; Czechoslovakia in 1948, the nearest case, turned on control of the police under the shadow of Soviet troops. Where the state had not broken and the army held — Germany in 1919 and 1923, Estonia in 1924, Indonesia in 1965, Sudan in 1971 — the attempt failed, usually within days.",
    against: { title: "Coups made to stop it", note: "The Cold War produced at least as many seizures against the left as by it. Several removed elected governments that were not communist at all.", ids: ["kornilov", "bulgaria23", "spain1936", "ajax", "guatemala", "baypigs", "brazil64", "g30s", "greece67", "lonnol", "chile73", "uruguay73", "videla"] },
